From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 08:02:40 -0300
Subject: power: supply: pmi8998_fg: keep an unknown status when the read fails

When reading the charger's status fails, the notifier sets the status
to unknown and then overwrites it with the property value, which the
failed read may have left unset.

Take the charger's status only when the read succeeded.

Signed-off-by: Fabricio Akio <fabricioakio@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/pmi8998_fg.c
@@ -524,8 +524,8 @@ static int pmi8998_fg_notifier_call(struct notifier_block *nb, unsigned long val
 						POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS, &propval);
 		if (ret)
 			chip->status = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_UNKNOWN;
-
-		chip->status = propval.intval;
+		else
+			chip->status = propval.intval;
 
 		power_supply_changed(chip->batt_psy);
 
-- 
